    {
      "id": "glyph-invariants",
      "label": "Invariants",
      "type": "content",
      "position": {
        "x": 120,
        "y": -440
      },
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 660,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Invariants\n\nA View may render glyph-shaped artwork without being an icon View. It is still a View representation. Every authored Surface starts with at least one View and ends in its ordinary Glyph; the terminal Glyph does not replace the View.\n\nThe terminal belongs to the selected track. Never select another Surface’s glyph merely because it appears first in the file."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-glyph",
          "nodeId": "glyph-invariants"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "glyph-contract",
      "label": "Contract",
      "type": "content",
      "position": {
        "x": -1000,
        "y": 300
      },
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 660,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Contract\n\nTypeGlyph reads named icon definitions `{kind: \"icon\", name}`, text/symbol definitions with value/symbol/name, as object definitions. Legacy graphs may contain bare strings, but TypeGlyph does not treat a bare string as an authored icon or symbol object. Text is limited to one grapheme by getSingleCharacterGlyph. Readers differ: surfaceChains extracts object glyph definitions; callers retain compatibility fallbacks. Do not assume every reader accepts every legacy form identically."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-glyph",
          "nodeId": "glyph-contract"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "glyph-ports",
      "label": "Ports and Relationships",
      "type": "content",
      "position": {
        "x": 120,
        "y": 300
      },
