      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Behavior\n\n## Implemented behavior\n\nTypeGlyph resolves known icon names and symbolic characters. collectSurfaceChains stops at the first Glyph and diagnoses continuation; resolveSurfaceGlyph selects the terminal mark and declared fallback.\n\n## Known gaps\n\nBare-string compatibility belongs to the concrete reader; current object-only extraction in surfaceChains means broad claims of universal string support need a dedicated regression. The smallest workspace representation’s interaction policy remains a product question, not a reason to add a title bar to Glyph.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nThe workspace interaction policy at terminal Glyph scale is still open. The accepted boundary is that glyph-shaped View artwork remains a View, and a terminal Glyph does not get a graph title bar. This spec does not decide new glyph zoom/navigation behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource (twilite repository):\n- `components/GraphEditor/components/TypeGlyph.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/glyphDefinition.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/surfaceChains.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/portDeclarations.js`\n\nFocused tests (twilite repository):\n- `tests/glyphDefinition.test.js`\n- `tests/surfaceChains.test.js`\n- `tests/hitboxGlyph.test.js`\n\nThese pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-glyph",
          "nodeId": "glyph-behavior"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "glyph-representations",
      "label": "Representations",
      "type": "content",
      "position": {
        "x": 120,
        "y": 1040
      },
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 660,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Representations\n\nA glyph is symbolic artwork. A View can render the same artwork while retaining View chrome and semantics. A selected representation uses the existing workspace frame. Surface, resolution and focus changes do not implicitly resize it, reflow neighbors or change camera zoom. Manual resizing is explicit. Internal nodes, edges, handles and pointer targets are clipped; exposed boundary controls remain accessible. Workspace title bars belong to View representations (including glyph-shaped artwork), not a terminal Glyph."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-glyph",
          "nodeId": "glyph-representations"
        }
      }
    },
